# Profile API Endpoints Tests

## Prerequisites
# 1. Start the backend server (mvn spring-boot:run)
# 2. Register a user and get an auth token
# 3. Replace {token} with your actual JWT token

## 1. Get Profile
GET http://localhost:8080/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Content-Type: application/json

###

## 2. Get Profile (compatibility endpoint)
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Content-Type: application/json

###

## 3. Update Profile (Full Update)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "heightCm": 175.5,
  "weightKg": 70.2,
  "gender": "male",
  "activityLevel": "moderately_active",
  "goal": "maintain",
  "age": 25,
  "locale": "en-US",
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "unitsPreference": "metric"
}

###

## 4. Partial Update Profile (PATCH)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "heightCm": 180.0,
  "weightKg": 75.0
}

###

## 5. Update Profile via compatibility endpoint
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "heightCm": 165.0,
  "weightKg": 55.0,
  "gender": "female",
  "goal": "lose"
}

###

## 6. Test Registration (to get a token)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User", 
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "testPassword123"
}

###

## 7. Test Login (to get a token)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "testPassword123"
}